    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d853">

                <pb facs="0789" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/322.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The General Receiver to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I understand from Falkner’s memorandum<anchor n="1" xml:id="d853-f1"/> that
                    German Receiver must be stationed permanently at or near Monrovia. Attitude
                    here, as stated by Minister Cromelin, is that receivers should rotate, and that
                    any other arrangement would be unfortunate. Am convinced that agreement
                    affecting German Receiver would necessarily become public eventually, and that
                    effect of such agreement would be to split receivership into two factions, thus
                    making success difficult. Await instructions in the premises.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
